<%# ONE LOOK'S CHARACTER MODEL, and the whole point of the layout is the arrow.

    The operator's acceptance test for this page was one sentence: "I want to see
    the images found on the internet and the output on the same UI." So the page is
    two panels with a direction between them — INPUT on the left, OUTPUT on the
    right, an arrow in the middle that turns downward when the panels stack. The
    relationship has to be readable without a caption, because the caption is what
    an operator skips.

    Numbered headings ("1 . Input", "2 . Output") carry the same job for a reader
    who lands mid-page on a phone, where the two panels are a scroll apart and the
    arrow is the only other thing saying which way the pipeline runs. %>
<div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-6 space-y-5">

  <%# WHO, and the way back. The person page is where every route to this one
      starts, so the breadcrumb is the return leg rather than decoration. %>
  <nav class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-2xs text-muted flex-wrap">
    <%= link_to "People", people_path, class: "hover:text-primary" %>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <%= link_to @person.full_name, person_path(@person.slug), class: "hover:text-primary" %>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span class="text-heading font-bold"><%= @appearance.descriptor %></span>
  </nav>

  <div class="card p-4 sm:p-5 flex gap-4 items-start">
    <div class="w-14 h-14 sm:w-16 sm:h-16 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-surface-alt border border-subtle
                overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
      <% avatar = @person.athlete_profile&.espn_headshot_url.presence || @person.avatar_url.presence %>
      <% if avatar %>
        <%= image_tag avatar, class: "object-cover w-full h-full", alt: @person.full_name %>
      <% else %>
        <span class="text-2xl opacity-40" aria-hidden="true">&#128100;</span>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
      <h1 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-heading truncate"><%= @person.full_name %></h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-secondary"><%= @appearance.descriptor %></p>
      <div class="flex gap-1.5 flex-wrap mt-2">
        <% if @appearance.default? %>
          <span class="badge text-3xs bg-success/10 text-success-ink border-success/40">default model</span>
        <% end %>
        <% if @appearance.colorway.present? %>
          <span class="badge text-3xs bg-surface-alt text-muted border-subtle"><%= @appearance.colorway %></span>
        <% end %>
        <span class="badge text-3xs bg-surface-alt text-muted border-subtle font-mono"><%= @appearance.slug %></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# THE TWO HALVES. 7 / 1 / 4 of twelve: the gallery is the panel that has to
      hold a grid of thumbnails, the identity is a handful of facts and a couple of
      buttons, and the middle column is the arrow. Stacks to one column below lg,
      where the arrow rotates.

      min-w-0 on both panels because a grid child defaults to min-content width,
      and one long unbroken URL inside would otherwise push the track wider than
      the viewport and give the whole page a horizontal scrollbar. %>
  <div class="grid gap-3 lg:gap-2 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">

    <section class="lg:col-span-7 min-w-0">
      <%= render "appearances/input_panel" %>
    </section>

    <%# THE ARROW SITS LEVEL WITH THE TWO HEADINGS, not with the middle of the row.
        Centring it vertically put it a thousand pixels below them on a populated
        gallery, where it reads as decoration between two unrelated cards rather
        than as the direction the pipeline runs. The top margin lands it beside the
        panel titles, which is where the eye is when it asks what connects them.

        lg:items-start on the grid is the other half: without it every cell
        stretches to the tallest, and the short output card grows a column of empty
        space as long as the gallery. %>
    <div data-test="pipeline-arrow" class="lg:col-span-1 flex items-center justify-center py-1 lg:mt-14"
         aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full border border-subtle bg-surface-alt text-primary
                  flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold shrink-0">
        <span class="lg:hidden">&darr;</span>
        <span class="hidden lg:inline">&rarr;</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="lg:col-span-4 min-w-0">
      <%= render "appearances/output_panel" %>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
